---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const updated = 'September 15, 2026';
---
<Base title="Cancellation & Refund Policy" description="How featured-listing subscriptions renew, how to cancel, and our refund policy for Hoarding Cleanup Finder.">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>Cancellation &amp; Refund Policy</h1>
    <p class="small">Last updated {updated}</p>

    <p>This policy explains how paid featured-listing subscriptions on Hoarding Cleanup Finder work — how they renew, how to cancel, and when refunds apply. It is part of our <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>. Free listings are always free and are not affected by this policy.</p>

    <h2>Plans and billing</h2>
    <p>A featured listing is a subscription, currently $49 per month or $399 per year. Payments are processed securely by Stripe. Your plan renews automatically at the end of each billing period — every month or every year, depending on the plan you chose — at the then-current price, until you cancel.</p>

    <h2>Automatic renewal</h2>
    <p>By subscribing you authorize us, through Stripe, to charge your payment method automatically at the start of each new billing period. We will email a receipt for each payment. You can cancel at any time to stop future renewals.</p>

    <h2>How to cancel</h2>
    <p>Sign in to your account, open <strong>Manage billing</strong>, and cancel there — this opens the Stripe billing portal, where you can cancel the subscription or update your card. You can also email <a href="mailto:hello@hoardingcleanupfinder.com">hello@hoardingcleanupfinder.com</a> and we will cancel it for you. Cancelling stops the next renewal; it does not trigger an immediate charge or an immediate refund.</p>

    <h2>What happens when you cancel</h2>
    <p>Your listing stays featured through the end of the period you have already paid for. When that period ends, the listing automatically reverts to a normal free listing. Nothing is deleted — your company stays in the directory, and you can turn the featured listing back on at any time.</p>

    <h2>Refunds</h2>
    <p>Because you keep the featured listing for the full period you paid for, we do not provide partial refunds for the unused part of a monthly or annual term after a cancellation. Two exceptions: if you were charged in error (for example, a duplicate charge or a charge after a confirmed cancellation), or if a technical problem on our side prevented your featured listing from displaying for a meaningful part of the period, contact us and we will make it right — that may be a credit or a refund, handled case by case. We may also grant a refund at our discretion where it is clearly fair.</p>

    <h2>Failed payments</h2>
    <p>If a renewal payment fails, Stripe will retry it over the following several days. If the payment still cannot be collected, the featured listing reverts to a free listing. Nothing is deleted, and you can re-subscribe at any time once your payment method is working.</p>

    <h2>Price changes</h2>
    <p>We may change subscription prices. Any change applies only to billing periods that start after we have given you notice; it never changes a period you have already paid for.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about billing, cancellation, or a refund? Email <a href="mailto:hello@hoardingcleanupfinder.com">hello@hoardingcleanupfinder.com</a> and we'll help.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
